BUFGCE_DIV with active CE or DIVIDE not 1 has BUFG driver  
The BUFGCE_DIV cell U_RTDS_FPGA_1G_INIT/U_BUFGCE_DIV_INIT U_RTDS_FPGA_1G_INIT/U_BUFGCE_DIV_INIT/I pin (and CE is ACTIVE or BUFGCE_DIVIDE is not 1) is driven by BUFGCE clock buffer u_clk_gen/clk_wiz_0_inst/inst/clkout3_buf. It should be reconnected in parallel to the driving clock buffer in order to reduce skew. Cascaded buffers introduce skew that can lead to difficult or impossible timing closure.
